  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1102 AM MDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nUpper high stays put over the Four Corners today through Tuesday. \nMostly dry conditions today with the exception of the Gila region. \nSlight uptick in storm chances with increasing coverage each day. \nThe Gila region will be favored again Monday afternoon for storms \nbut may even see storms get triggered off the west slopes of the \nSacramento Mtns as well as more activity closer towards the AZ \nborder. Blowing dust possible over the Lordsburg Playa tomorrow \nafternoon. Similar conditions and locations for storms Tuesday with \nthe focus over the area mountains and locations west of the Rio \nGrande. The aforementioned upper high dissolves Tuesday, but starts \nto shift over to the Gulf and Gulf states Wednesday and onward. This \nwill be more of a classic monsoonal tap of moisture funneling into \nthe area. Better chances and coverage of thunderstorms during this \ntime frame with flash flooding being the main hazard.",
